{"name":"Blue Dude","hex":"#4a5c94","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"dude","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A man, generally a younger man.","A term of address for someone, often but not exclusively a man, particularly when hailing, cautioning them or offering advice."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A term of address, usually for a man, conveying awe, excitement, surprise, annoyance, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dude"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dude","blocks":[{"text":"Dude is American slang for an individual, typically male. From the 1870s to the 1960s, dude primarily meant a male person who dressed in an extremely fashionable manner or a conspicuous citified person who was visiting a rural location, a \"city slicker\". In the 1960s, dude evolved to mean any male person, a meaning that slipped into mainstream American slang in the 1970s. Current slang retains at least some use of all three of these common meanings."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dude","wikidata":"Q942988"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/Berry-wall-king-dudes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/Berry-wall-king-dudes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Evander Berry Wall, a New York socialite, was dubbed \"King of the Dudes\". He is pictured (1888) in the New York American newspaper at the time of the \"battle of the Dudes\".[3][4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerry-wall-king-dudes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/1883_-_origin_of_dude_-_Chicago_Tribune_-_25_Feb_1883.jpg/500px-1883_-_origin_of_dude_-_Chicago_Tribune_-_25_Feb_1883.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/1883_-_origin_of_dude_-_Chicago_Tribune_-_25_Feb_1883.jpg/1280px-1883_-_origin_of_dude_-_Chicago_Tribune_-_25_Feb_1883.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/1883_-_origin_of_dude_-_Chicago_Tribune_-_25_Feb_1883.jpg/500px-1883_-_origin_of_dude_-_Chicago_Tribune_-_25_Feb_1883.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Among the first published descriptions defining \"dude\"; Chicago Tribune, 25 February 1883","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1883_-_origin_of_dude_-_Chic